From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nds-ports <nds-ports@localhost>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:12:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Clip wall posts taller than the view in one step

ScalePost stepped through every pixel below the view to find the texel
at its bottom edge, which for walls right in front of the player is
most of the time spent drawing: a wall filling ten times the view
height stepped through nine view heights per column. The texel and
step counter are now computed at once, with the same result.
---
 wl_draw.c | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/wl_draw.c b/wl_draw.c
index 5dd58a5..1dad953 100644
--- a/wl_draw.c
+++ b/wl_draw.c
@@ -322,15 +322,17 @@ void ScalePost (void)
     yendoffs = centery + ywcount - 1;
     yw=TEXTURESIZE-1;
 
-    while(yendoffs >= viewheight)
+    // Skip the pixels below the view at once, like stepping through them
+    if(yendoffs >= viewheight)
     {
-        ywcount -= TEXTURESIZE/2;
-        while(ywcount <= 0)
+        ywcount -= TEXTURESIZE/2 * (yendoffs - viewheight + 1);
+        if(ywcount <= 0)
         {
-            ywcount += yd;
-            yw--;
+            int steps = -ywcount / yd + 1;
+            ywcount += steps * yd;
+            yw -= steps;
         }
-        yendoffs--;
+        yendoffs = viewheight - 1;
     }
     if(yw < 0) return;
 
